\begin{abstract}
%  Efficient processing of large-scale data streams is essential for applications in networking, databases, and data mining. Traditional sketch algorithms often face trade-offs between memory efficiency and key recording accuracy, particularly in high-speed environments. This paper introduces \textbf{Hidden Sketch}, a novel invertible data structure designed to record keys and frequencies with minimal memory overhead. Hidden Sketch integrates a Count-Min(CM) Sketch for frequency encoding and a Reversible Bloom Filter for key encoding, achieving robust decoding and high accuracy. To complete tasks such as heavy hitter detection and heavy change detection, this paper proposes a two-stage framework: a lightweight cold filter to prune insignificant data and a Hidden Sketch for precise recoding, significantly reducing computational and memory overhead. Theoretical analysis proves its superior memory efficiency, and experimental evaluations demonstrate that it achieves up to 65\% lower memory memory usage and order-of-magnitude improvements in accuracy compared to prior approaches, making it a scalable and reliable solution for data stream processing.
  Modern data stream applications demand memory-efficient solutions for accurately tracking frequent items, such as heavy hitters and heavy changers, under strict resource constraints. Traditional sketches face inherent accuracy-memory trade-offs: they either lose precision to reduce memory usage or inflate memory costs to enable high recording capacity. This paper introduces Hidden Sketch, a space-efficient reversible data structure for key and frequency encoding. Our design uniquely combines a Reversible Bloom Filter (RBF) and a Count-Min (CM) Sketch for invertible key and frequency storage, enabling precise reconstruction for both keys and their frequencies with minimal memory. Theoretical analysis establishes Hidden Sketch's space complexity and guaranteed reversibility, while extensive experiments demonstrate its substantial improvements in accuracy and space efficiency in frequent item tracking tasks. By eliminating the trade-off between reversibility and space efficiency, Hidden Sketch provides a scalable foundation for real-time stream analytics in resource-constrained environments.
\end{abstract}

