 A \emph{vertex ranking} of a graph $G=(V,E)$ is a coloring $c: V \rightarrow [k]$ such that for any two distinct vertices $x$ and $y$, and for every simple path $P$ from $x$ to $y$, if $c(x)=c(y)$, then there exists an internal vertex $z$ in $P$ such that $c(x)<c(z)$. 
The \emph{vertex ranking number} of $G$ is the smallest integer $k$ such that $G$ admits a vertex ranking using only $k$ colors.



