For each point $p\in\P\cap s$,  consider a translated copy ${\bm\sigma'}({p})$ of $-\sigma$, centered at  $p$. Now due to Lemma~\ref{clm:ext}, if {$\bm{\sigma'}(o_{\tau})\cap \partial {\bm\sigma'}(p)\cap \interior{(Cell(p))}$} is non-empty, then $p$ is an element of $V_{s,\tau}$.

