 Let ${\bf{A}}=\left(a_{ij}\right)_{t\times t}$ be a {$t\times t$} partition (see Figure~\ref{fig:disk}). Let $\bf{a_i}'$ and $\bf{A_j}$ denotes the $i$th row and $j$th column of $\bf{A}$. We use $a_{ij}$ to denote a tile in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, where $i,j\in[t]$. W.l.o.g., we assume that the object $\sigma$ intersects a tile in both $\bf{a_1}'$ and $\bf{A_1}$. 

