Instruct-MusicGen~\cite{zhang2024instruct} fine-tunes MusicGen, enabling music editing with text prompts. MusicGen-style~\cite{rouard2024audio} trains MusicGen from scratch, incorporating a text conditioner and an audio feature extractor to fuse text and audio during inference. 

\textbf{Training-time control with local conditions.}
For more granular controls, MusicGen~\cite{musicgen} prepends a melody-based conditioning tensor (along with text embeddings) and trains the entire model from scratch. Similarly, JASCO~\cite{tal2024joint} appends all conditions to the model’s input across the feature dimension but also requires training from scratch—demanding significant computational resources and making it less flexible to add new conditions. MusiConGen~\cite{musicongen} and Coco-Mulla~\cite{lin2023content} fine-tune MusicGen, enabling chord and rhythm conditions without full retraining. 
