Motivated by recent advances, this work develops and analyzes a mixed FEM for unsteady convective $p$-type Brinkman-Forchheimer flow coupled with a transport equation. The formulation introduces pseudostress, concentration gradient, and a Lagrange multiplier as additional unknowns alongside velocity and concentration. Raviart-Thomas elements and standard polynomials are used for spatial discretization, with backward Euler in time. The fully discrete scheme is high-order, implicit, and unconditionally stable. Under small data assumptions, we prove existence, uniqueness, and derive optimal error estimates. This appears to be the first analysis of a lowest-order mixed FEM for time-dependent Brinkman-Forchheimer flow models.


