where $E_{\widetilde{\Gamma}} : H^{1/2}(\widetilde{\Gamma}) \to H^{1/2}(\Gamma)$ is a bounded extension operator. For instance, if $v \in H^{1/2}(\widetilde{\Gamma})$, we define its extension as $E_{\widetilde{\Gamma}}(v) := z|_{\Gamma}$, where $z$ is the unique solution to
