Let \( (\bz_h^n, \chi_h^n)\in \mathbf{V}_{h}\times\mathrm{Q} \) for \( n=1,\dots,N \). As in the continuous case, testing \eqref{eq:dis.sub1} with \( (\bta_h , \bv_{h}) := (\bsi_{h,\star}^{n},\bu_{h,\star}^{n}) \in \mathbb{H}_h \times \mathbf{V}_h \) and using the discrete inf-sup condition for \( \mathscr{B}^F \) (cf.~\eqref{eq:dis.inf.b}) yields
	\begin{equation}\label{eq:dis.j1}
		\begin{array}{c}
			\dfrac{1}{2\Delta t}\left(\Vert \bu_{h,\star}^n\Vert_{0,\Omega}^{2}-\Vert \bu_{h,\star}^{n-1}\Vert_{0,\Omega}^{2}\right)\,+\,\dfrac{1}{\nu}\, \Vert \bdev(\bsi_{h,\star}^{n})\Vert_{0,\Omega}^{2}
			\,\leq\, c_{\mathscr{F}^F}\left(\Vert\mathbf{g}^n\Vert_{1/2,\Gamma_{\mathtt{o}}^c}+a_1\Vert\chi_h^n\Vert_{\mathrm{Q}}\right)\Vert\bsi_{h,\star}^{n}\Vert_{\mathbb{H}}
			\\ \,+\,\Big(\dfrac{1}{\nu}\Vert\bz_{h}^n\Vert_{\mathbf{V}}\,\Vert\bdev(\bsi_{h,\star}^{n})\Vert_{0,\Omega}
			\,+\,|\Omega|^{(4-p)/4}\Vert\bz_{h}^n\Vert_{\mathbf{V}}^{p-2}\Vert\bu_{h,\star}^{n}\Vert_{\mathbf{V}}\Big)\Vert\bu_{h,\star}^{n}\Vert_{\mathbf{V}}\,.
