\section{Numerical results}\label{sec.7}
We present two test cases to evaluate the method. The first, with a manufactured solution, confirms the convergence rates of Theorem~\ref{theorem-rates-of-convergence}; the second, inspired by reverse osmosis, lacks an exact solution. Both are implemented in $\mathtt{FreeFem}$++, using the decoupling strategy from Section~\ref{s:4}. Iterations stop when the global \( \ell^2 \)-norm of the update falls below a set tolerance. Errors are defined by
