	In this subsection, we evaluate the effectiveness of latent reward generation in \textbf{DRAE (ours)} and its ability to generate reliable reward signals that align with human-labeled rewards.
	\subsubsection{Experimental Setup}
	We perform a comprehensive evaluation comparing the latent rewards generated by language models (LLMs) to human-labeled rewards for multiple robotic tasks. The evaluation procedure is as follows:

	\subsubsection{Methodology}
	1. Human experts manually annotate reward signals for each task.
	2. Latent rewards are generated using task descriptions processed by LLMs in \textbf{DRAE (ours)}.
	3. We compare the generated reward signals with human-labeled rewards across the following dimensions:
	- \textbf{Correlation coefficient}: Measures the similarity between latent and human-labeled rewards.
	- \textbf{Reward signal stability}: Assesses the consistency of the reward signals across different task executions.
	- \textbf{Policy performance variance}: Evaluates how stable the policy's performance is under varying reward signals.

