\section{Related Work}
\label{sec:related work}
\subsection{Diffusion Models}
%扩散模型是一类新兴的深度生成模型，在图像合成、视频生成、图像修复等多个应用领域展现出突破性的表现。其核心原理是模拟物理过程中的扩散现象：逐步向数据添加噪声，将其转化为噪声状态，随后通过逆过程将其还原到原始数据。最初，Ho等人引入了去噪扩散概率模型（DDPM），为后续研究奠定了基础。随后，xxx等人提出了潜在扩散模型方法，大幅降低了计算复杂度并提高了效率，进一步推动了扩散模型的发展，扩散模型领域由此涌现出大量创新方法[参考文献]。在本文中，我们的框架同样采用基于扩散的水印技术，利用其内在的鲁棒性和安全性来增强我们提出的多模态水印方法。

Diffusion models \cite{nichol2021improved}\cite{song2019generative}\cite{song2020score} are a class of emerging deep generative models that have demonstrated groundbreaking performance in various applications, such as image synthesis \cite{dhariwal2021diffusion}\cite{saharia2022photorealistic}\cite{ramesh2022hierarchical}, video generation \cite{ho2022imagen}\cite{ho2022video}, and image restoration \cite{saharia2022image}\cite{wang2022zero}\cite{kawar2022denoising}. The core principle of these models is to simulate the physical diffusion process: noise is incrementally added to the data, transforming it into a noisy state, which can then be reconstructed back to its original form through a reverse process. Initially, Ho et al. \cite{ho2020denoising} introduced the denoising diffusion probabilistic model (DDPM), which laid the groundwork for subsequent research \cite{lyu2019advances}\cite{gu2022vector}\cite{lu2022dpm}. Later, Rombach et al. \cite{rombach2022high} proposed latent diffusion models, significantly reducing computational complexity and improving efficiency, thus further advancing the development of diffusion models \cite{kim2022diffusionclip}\cite{meng2021sdedit}\cite{tang2023emergent}. This progress has spurred a wave of innovation within the diffusion model community, leading to many new approaches. \cite{gandikota2023erasing}\cite{wang2024patch} In this paper, our proposed framework also leverages diffusion-based watermarking techniques, harnessing their inherent robustness and security benefits to strengthen our multi-modal watermarking method.




\subsection{Image Watermarking}
%图像-文本水印技术，作为一种将文本信息嵌入图像的信息隐藏手段，主要用于在图像中嵌入版权信息、认证数据或其他敏感文本，以便实现追踪、验证和版权保护。在计算机视觉领域，数字水印技术的嵌入历史悠久，传统方法如xx等，通过图像的频域转换实现隐形水印的构建。随着生成式模型的快速发展，尤其是Diffusion模型在人工智能生成内容（AIGC）领域的显著进展，其在快速生成图像的能力不仅推动了信息传播的便捷性，也带来了知识产权保护的新挑战。因此，图像-文本水印技术在应对这些挑战的同时，也迎来了新的发展机遇。黄等人提出了一种可以直接应用于扩散模型生成后的自适应图像水印方法，Zhu等人提出了一种基于对抗性训练的水印嵌入方式。它们有效增强了水印的鲁棒性和不可感知性，但此类后处理方法仍旧会对图像质量产生较大影响。最近的一些工作，如 Stable Signature 和 A Recipe for Watermarking Diffusion Models，尝试在扩散生成过程中嵌入水印，以减少对图像质量的影响，但这些方法仅支持提取固定的水印信息。另一些创新的研究，如 Tree-Ring，通过调整潜在表示来嵌入版权信息，从而省去了训练的成本，但该方法仅能实现版权保护，无法传递更丰富的信息。即使是最新的模型（如 GAUS），其有效信息的传输也仅限于约512位。因此，目前图像-文本水印的信息容量受限，阻碍了其更高密度的内容传输。
Image-text watermarking technology \cite{ahmadi2020redmark}\cite{liu2024mirror}, as a means of embedding textual information within images, is primarily used to insert copyright details, authentication data, or other sensitive text for tracking, verification, and copyright protection purposes. 
% With the rapid development of generative models, particularly the progress of Diffusion models in AI-generated content (AIGC), these models not only enhance the ease of information dissemination with their capability for rapid image generation but also present new challenges for intellectual property protection.
Huang et al. \cite{huang2019enhancing} proposed an adaptive image watermarking method that can be directly applied to the outputs of diffusion models. Zhu et al. \cite{Zhu2018HiDDeNHD} introduced a watermark embedding approach based on adversarial training. these methods effectively enhance the robustness and imperceptibility of the watermark, but like other post-processing techniques, it can still significantly affect image quality. Recent approaches, such as the Stable Signature method \cite{fernandez2023stable} and the method proposed by Zhao et al. \cite{zhao2023recipe}, attempt to embed watermarks during the diffusion generation process to mitigate impacts on image quality. However, these methods only allow the extraction of fixed watermark information. Other innovative studies, such as the Tree-ring method \cite{wen2023tree}, aim to embed copyright information by modifying latent representations, thereby eliminating training costs; however, this approach only achieves copyright protection without enabling the transmission of meaningful information. Even the latest models, such as Gaussian Shading \cite{yang2024gaussian}, are limited to transmitting approximately 512 bits of effective information. Consequently, the bit limitations of image-text watermarks restrict the density of content they can carry.



