\section{Conclusion}

In this paper, we propose a multi-modal watermarking framework by integrating text content watermarking and image content watermarking into a unified system, introducing a novel multi-modal watermarking content method. This method leverages vector discretization in encoder-based vector quantization to achieve mutual transformation between text content watermarks and image content watermarks, addressing a key limitation in existing technologies. The inclusion of a restoration module effectively mitigates accuracy loss caused by various attacks, significantly enhancing the robustness of the watermark while maintaining the integrity of the image content. Experimental results demonstrate that the method exhibits strong resistance to almost all noise attacks, making it a secure and scalable solution for digital copyright protection.


% In the future, we will explore the possibility of embedding more larger-scale secret images within the current constraints of watermark length to enhance the richness and precision of content when transforming text watermarks into image watermarks. Additionally, we aim to further optimize the balance between watermark capacity and image quality,  thereby improving the framework's applicability across a broader range of applications.






