\section{Experimental Results}
\label{sec:exp}
We perform the simulation for 4000 agents across a week. All agents are powered by GPT-4o except when specified otherwise. Human parameters and personas for each agent were initialized using answers from our proprietary dataset.

\subsection{Human Likeness}
A central question is: How accurately do synthetic residents replicate the behaviors of real humans? To answer this question, we input the agent actions to ChatGPT-4o \cite{king2023conversation} to assess whether agent interactions appear human or AI-generated using a 5-point Likert scale, with higher scores indicating a stronger resemblance to human-like responses. We further report in Table \ref{table:human_like} the human-likeliness scores averaged across interactions, comparing our method with the baseline \cite{uist/ParkOCMLB23}, AGA \cite{corr/abs-2402-02053}, and HumanoidAgent \cite{emnlp/WangCC23}. Our model achieves the highest score, demonstrating its ability to generate behaviors that closely resemble real human actions. An example of daily interactions is shown in Appendix \ref{sec:action_example}.

