\subsection{Venue Heatmap}

Understanding crowd distribution patterns is essential for urban planning and resource allocation. Figure \ref{fig:traffic} illustrates the crowd distribution trends over time. Between 22:00 and 06:00, most agents remain at home for rest. On weekdays, employed agents typically work in offices until the evening, after which many engage in recreational activities such as visiting sports centers or pursuing hobbies. In contrast, weekends exhibit a more diverse distribution, with agents visiting venues for entertainment and relaxation. This pattern aligns with natural human tendencies, where individuals gather in leisure spaces during non-working hours, mirroring real-world crowd behavior.


