\begin{abstract}
% Code Large Language Models (CodeLLMs) have become essential for modern software development, yet efficiently serving them in resource-constrained environments remains challenging. Current LLM serving systems rely on static batch size configurations that fail to adapt to the dynamic and heterogeneous nature of coding workloads, resulting in frequent SLA violations and degraded performance.
