\subsubsection{UM-Bridge on HPC systems}

UM-Bridge also includes support for SLURM or PBS based \gls{HPC} systems. In this case, a custom component takes UM-Bridge evaluation requests from the client and translates those into jobs managed by HyperQueue \cite{HyperQueue}. HyperQueue then acts as the load balancer, spawning model instances as \gls{HPC} scheduler jobs and passing evaluation requests to them as needed.

Models may be local installations of the simulation software
or containerized versions. %RS for ease of use. 
