\section{Outlook}

We aim to establish UM-Bridge across the \gls{UQ} community, serving as a catalyst for highly efficient \gls{UQ} methods applied to challenging problems, and acting as a link between \gls{UQ} and applications as well as between academia and industry. With growing computational resources and the advance of science, we expect growing complexity in \gls{UQ} applications, making the need for separation of concerns and advanced \gls{UQ} tools even more prominent.


