\section{Experiment Set Up}\label{app:setup}
\textbf{Datasets.}
We evaluate the capabilities of our method across multiple datasets. For integrating internal/external knowledge task, we employ the ConFiQA For  retrieval-augmented general tasks ,we use HotpotQA \cite{yang2018hotpotqa}, 2WikiMultiHopQA \cite{ho2020constructing} and Musique \cite{trivedi2022musique}. 

\textbf{Training.}
We conduct experiments with \texttt{Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct} and \texttt{Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct}, We use five retrieved passages to all retrieval-based methods. For  integrating internal/external knowledge task, we reconstruct the ConFiQA dataset for training and testing. As for retrieval-augmented general tasks training, we use the training sets of  HotpotQA to form a unified dataset for \method and other fine-tuning-based baselines. For the SFT baselines, we train all models for one epoch. For GRPO based baselines and our \method, we use  a global batch size of 8, a rollout batch size of 16, a rollout temperature of 0.9, and a learning rate of $1\times10^{-6}$.All experiments are conducted using 8 A100 GPUs and share the same system prompt for training and inference.

% \textbf{Baselines.}
% To evaluate the effectiveness of \method, we compare it against the following baseline methods:\\Inference without Retrieval: Direct inference and inference with reasoning .Inference with Retrieval: Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). Fine-Tuning-Based Methods: Supervised fine-tuning (SFT) ,Supervised fine-tuning (SFT) with RAG context, GRPO and GRPO with RAG context.\\


\section{Evaluation} \label{app:in-ex}
For RAG generate capability. We use Exact Match (EM) as the evaluation metric following \cite{jin2025search}Evaluation is conducted on the test or validation sets of all datasets to assess both in-domain and out-of-domain performance. For  integrating parametric/contextual knowledge task, We adopted EM and self-defined metrics to evaluate the model's ability to utilize parametric and contextual knowledge.

\section{Further Experiments}\label{app:exp}
