    \caption{Visualization of a coupled $\delta$-visiting order. Edges are drawn between vertices $P(i)$ and $Q(j)$, when one is a $\delta$-signature vertex and $|P(i)-Q(j)|\leq \delta$. Then, a coupled $\delta$-visiting order consists of a subset of the drawn edges, shown as an orange bipartite graph, where no two edges cross and it contains one incident edge for every $\delta$-signature vertex.}
