\abstract{To enable precise and fully automated cell type annotation with large language models (LLMs), we developed a graph-structured feature–marker database to retrieve entities linked to differential genes for cell reconstruction. We further designed a multi-task workflow to optimize the annotation process. Compared to general-purpose LLMs, our method improves human evaluation scores by up to 0.21 and semantic similarity by 6.1\% across 11 tissue types, while more closely aligning with the cognitive logic of manual annotation.}

\keywords{Cell type annotation, Graph RAG, Large language models, Graph data curation, Multi-task workflow, scRNA-seq}

% For precise fully automated cell type annotation with large language models (LLMs), we constructed a feature–marker graph database for retrieval cell features associated with differentially expressed marker genes. Additionally, we designed a multi-agent workflow to refine the entire annotation process. Compared to existing methods, our pipeline delivers higher annotation accuracy while aligning more closely with the cognitive logic of manual annotation, which improves the credibility of AI-driven cell type annotation.

