\section{Method}
%In this section, we approach LTAR through a causal perspective using a SCM illustrated in Figure ~\ref{fig3}. While intrinsic causal mechanisms can be established when cross-modal biases and visual confounders are known, their unobservability poses significant challenges. To address this, we propose the \textbf{C}ross-\textbf{M}odal \textbf{D}ual-\textbf{C}ausal \textbf{L}earning (CMDCL) framework (Figure ~\ref{fig4}), which models and mitigates these biases and confounders, enabling more robust representation learning for LTAR.

